    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28443" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δροσ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bedew, besprinkle,</i> in 
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				1312
			</span></i> (lyr.), prob. in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hyps.Fr.</u>
				9.4
			</span></i>:—later in 
				Act.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Posidon.
				20
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				12.16
			</span></i>:— 
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Ulc.</u>
				12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεδροσισμένον νέφος</span>”
				<i>dewy,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.L.
					7.152
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡνίκ᾽ ἂν ὑπὸ τοῦ οἴνου δροσισθῇ
					ἡ ψυχή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epict.
					<u>Gnom.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<i>form dew,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				939b38
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δροσίζων ἱδρώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herod.Med.
				</span></i>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.Mus.</u>
				58.99
			</span></i>; <i>to be in a flaccid condition,</i> of the body, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Gym.</u>
				48
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Archig.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				6.3
			</span></i>.</div>
